#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157000 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "332b1d25-852f-51ad-9a38-62b562ae247f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12522" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(\\pi,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n![](images/50/5018652c7049be48f998af2ceac522f4170475b1e5f5ed6b2daf77d1443eab27.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/9e/9ecc6bbb35ec3b1fc94b49a9da87099480dccbf63447ecd18b812547110b35ef.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/92/92a91186756bb96fcf826be1ac0819b1a1fc7660cbf8ebff300d6e9390f90416.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/4a/4a0d68e1fb2aa93a6e7606cf7c96dcf692d366a0571c36e589810a4276572339.svg)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](images/b9/b93095604beb468dac2fd708fa679379fdcdf273be6ae6a74517ec605e96a88b.svg) \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = e^y\\cos x ,  \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} =e^y\\sin x .\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\pi,0).$ This gives\n\n![](images/16/168592a2f48649e0cd90aa5226a55204435a02477b9f54f09fc22db32327d7b1.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157001 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523" :question/problem "Given that \n![](images/43/43ec08d3ac9a00921335912f8e2cf8770397f141b4eebbb4f857fd0be69f7441.svg) \n evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/39/398ea92d21b959026a702db0f606915acb31906451a9039925518ca79fa89717.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/5e/5ea286680d2cec429fe920628617d083f47dd53519c2d40f30115dee45a18bc3.svg)\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det \\left( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\right)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/14/1488754e319066706880b21fd4642c7b6a75a458770cab254b974b13d35425a2.svg)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](images/c9/c92e0f35c58187af3fe961947e6e96f0cd82cf32bb00cfd4f51ca3c742339e0c.svg) we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\ln y, \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y})=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1) = 0 \\cdot 0 - 1\\cdot 1 = -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157002 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)  = x^2 e^y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/f2/f2e3cce8b785350e4a3d746dfbbb1e805cc490c5a28680a59bb22e266b9c6b48.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/43/43938aea0610386ae1e7cd862b234b326a396a3c06df1cd8d63ba568c9bd5d62.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/81/81b814aff57a058f564080308dd8fbe220994cf0dcbd84b80715ded32c5c96a1.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $\\left(1,0\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5dbce3-5eeb-5299-a81b-71b95b40a702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435379} {:answer/id #uuid "533319f1-cf66-5e55-a50b-27c89a39ea11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435382} {:answer/id #uuid "afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435386} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6b5589-dee3-5358-89b2-bb7e5109233c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435388} {:answer/id #uuid "f224da51-5558-5714-9c8e-ab71238f6195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afde4582-cdac-5bc3-b210-1397789ef534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435386} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0eb9da-e4d5-55d6-ad33-7db8760cccce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d48bb18b-a23a-5640-ba69-c0db05f527bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-102452" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(2,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2xy & 2y-{x}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2xy)=-2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-{x}^{2})=-2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy)=-2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-{x}^{2})=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2y & -2x \\\\ -2x & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(2,1).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(2,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d5c0268-7cc2-5ad3-8272-4c515f0a750d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236311} {:answer/id #uuid "62148d00-7a55-50e2-b711-77a971693980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236437} {:answer/id #uuid "894ef656-89f8-5a8c-8406-3d578e81891c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236677} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b8f68b-a298-5bdf-932f-025f3b453029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237167} {:answer/id #uuid "fe41e0d7-e1ef-5547-ac3c-3ee0657660a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d5c0268-7cc2-5ad3-8272-4c515f0a750d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236311} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fbb1a14-9bc3-5e31-8398-a65b4f534a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b064463-cab9-5bec-b4bd-67252dafbaa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-102477" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y-2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2xy)=-2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-{x}^{2})=1-2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2xy)=1-2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{x}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2y & 1-2x \\\\ 1-2x & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1,2)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435375} {:answer/id #uuid "1d97894b-06e8-5458-afce-3b6280583bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435377} {:answer/id #uuid "49af7f88-d313-53b2-a836-26eef4f823e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435381} {:answer/id #uuid "6341ade3-f46e-594c-b2db-483df7d6f5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435383} {:answer/id #uuid "e9393f5b-f485-5c2a-b52d-4ac15221029b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "012e8862-6d84-5ca3-808d-e580b5b68412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435375} :answer-field/id #uuid "835cf471-5984-50ad-ac7a-5c92395f40c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e525b492-a29a-585f-8c96-2055a51f2341" :question/math-academy-id "q-102686" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y{x}^{2}-1\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{x}^{2}-1)=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2{x}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,-1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,-1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62d58fc9-233d-5a98-9f47-8a3790a441f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236443} {:answer/id #uuid "804c671d-3217-5280-aa02-fe2a73812ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236615} {:answer/id #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236672} {:answer/id #uuid "944e0f31-80d6-5eac-8960-7ada905bec43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236758} {:answer/id #uuid "d93bce69-5901-5324-bd97-83116ddf04a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236672} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c1b5e6-8017-5a27-ad73-0d376c902134" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba2b3d0e-8f3a-5211-b064-2ffdb4af104d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102688" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(\\pi ,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{bmatrix},$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(\\pi ,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\pi ,-1)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(\\pi ,-1)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33bfe849-177a-595a-a0ab-0f31871be845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389423} {:answer/id #uuid "506fbdd5-6f95-50b7-bf79-a8e6f12af0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 20 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389424} {:answer/id #uuid "22530ff9-8ee1-5653-9189-7257b61c3df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 10 \\\\ 10 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389425} {:answer/id #uuid "7e72de7a-05de-51d7-9a04-70e16f91e383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389426} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4b43e7-24cc-5566-83a4-12233460ad1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c4b43e7-24cc-5566-83a4-12233460ad1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389427} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf7a152-c075-537f-98b6-31165d39d652" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80f3f97d-e5ae-5fea-a537-3ca9f7c75a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163637" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{bmatrix},$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=10xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=5{x}^{2}-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy)=10y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=10x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy)=10x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}10y & 10x \\\\ 10x & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae64ecf2-f100-5ee1-bf22-d62f17c06d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155662} {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155663} {:answer/id #uuid "30a4bd7f-a653-586c-8d6c-48bbd5f3eadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + x \\\\ \\cos y + x & \\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155664} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54a19a-e583-584b-a065-7c3d2342cae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & x\\cos y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155665} {:answer/id #uuid "7613ab91-83d0-595d-baf0-b61833c485f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155666}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5f160e6d-8669-5f1d-a718-6927812f7f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48011387-df7d-5d71-b876-3df593d3bf4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394100} {:answer/id #uuid "b379f4c6-96cf-5dd6-9925-574eea16f8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394101} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3f1c3c-63fa-5e17-875f-c1a698e0f6ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x & \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394102} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9bcc3c-bd3b-5708-8734-2c02467d117b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394103} {:answer/id #uuid "3213b7e4-ef64-5dfb-891d-c56e3a6c1087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f9bcc3c-bd3b-5708-8734-2c02467d117b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394103} :answer-field/id #uuid "35959f64-1830-5289-be56-634cfb3973ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fc495d4-08fa-5ada-9f41-a42761e42726" :question/math-academy-id "q-80939" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce37079c-2eca-52cb-9217-b5bdc1cb43b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3x^{2} - y & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155668} {:answer/id #uuid "d8df90ee-e70b-544e-ad57-b2bdf4264fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3x^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155669} {:answer/id #uuid "10fc1fef-463d-5b7a-bbce-4dff18dc6262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155670} {:answer/id #uuid "3e3bd1d3-1790-5ddf-8382-84e4bdacfcc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3x^{2} - y & -1 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155671} {:answer/id #uuid "44242b8b-5a8c-532a-847c-6076d5352455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6x & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155672}] :answer-field/id #uuid "12293606-e74e-5b3d-b6fa-1d12e5769093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155667}] :question/id #uuid "67d83888-c95f-5ab0-a4ad-e179570526ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-80940" :question/problem "Find $f^{″}(x, y)$ for the function $f(x, y)$ given that\n$f^{′}(x, y) = \\begin{bmatrix}3x^{2} - y & -x\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fac2aac-15fd-5b1a-8c19-cdbaaa605b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155674} {:answer/id #uuid "af2543c6-e121-548c-9ce8-bd9e83f27959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155675} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1bd87c-c87b-5317-bf18-04917ad67fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155676} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd64df2-e5b8-5aaa-a2df-8978d2413927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155677} {:answer/id #uuid "540f5941-edc3-564d-ab1c-16a630b65ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd64df2-e5b8-5aaa-a2df-8978d2413927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155677} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7f08daa-f6b4-563b-b34a-95db72823c43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56bfdc28-d81a-5ee4-a9f9-1fab676af72b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80944" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},$\nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{3})=2{y}^{3}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{3} & 6x{y}^{2} \\\\ 6x{y}^{2} & 6{x}^{2}y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=2\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=-24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc2fb431-06b2-541f-bd81-028b0e746c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394114} {:answer/id #uuid "d1434c5a-b907-5ee4-aa01-b0af306c1b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394115} {:answer/id #uuid "58d1bc29-616a-542c-9866-77f1468c9682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394116} {:answer/id #uuid "1ff0187a-1203-58bf-b9e9-849dddbc8237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394117} {:answer/id #uuid "0646bfe4-8821-5269-85bc-ca35307c912f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc2fb431-06b2-541f-bd81-028b0e746c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394114} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b5b2192-3f70-59ee-87fd-c98b6a39c105" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52b9f18b-c40a-5c3f-88f5-e136ad636bb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-81009" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-4y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}-4x-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4y+1)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4y+1)=-4\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a863fee-48cb-518a-94c7-332f0d5dfb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348671} {:answer/id #uuid "236352e1-e284-5137-93e8-01d0c0b82dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348749} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6da9cd-0b80-5391-a066-ff87ff441cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350254} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b5d5ad-403a-5e9b-b47e-9495ed54eecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350322} {:answer/id #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f56bbbf-1a13-5c6d-a2d7-69c5469daa32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0dab700a-fa4f-5675-9473-37a2b428ee20" :question/math-academy-id "q-81023" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2(x-1){y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2(x-1)^{2}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=4(x-1)y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=4(x-1)y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4(x-1)y \\\\ 4(x-1)y & 2(x-1)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c42b794-72d6-514f-85b6-40ef2b7dcd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348690} {:answer/id #uuid "3454730a-5aab-57e6-8c0f-17209a604055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348916} {:answer/id #uuid "7b479b77-d903-5f0c-8f7d-530e7863b915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349579} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f41cb7-2e5a-5303-bc84-7130dab8c440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350611} {:answer/id #uuid "fb35d3bb-cccc-50cf-84a5-4d39d7149a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb35d3bb-cccc-50cf-84a5-4d39d7149a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350661} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb30829b-8d9a-5a87-b3fc-44d8886af1ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0469958-83f9-5c79-aae7-bbff4a96354f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81123" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=(y-1)({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1))\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x(y-1) & {x}^{2}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(y-1))=2(y-1)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-1)=2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(y-1))=2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2(y-1) & 2x \\\\ 2x & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1,2)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
